---

<BaseLayout
  title="Solihull PHV Test — Frequently Asked Questions"
  description="Solihull PHV test FAQs: how many questions, the pass mark, key questions, DBS and medical requirements, retakes, and how to prepare for the taxi badge test."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <main class="md:flex md:justify-center">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-[750px]">
      <h1>Solihull PHV Test — Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

      <p>
        Quick answers to the questions drivers ask most about the
        <strong>Solihull PHV test</strong> and the licensing process behind
        it. For the full picture, see our guides on
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/solihull/how-to-pass/"
          >passing the Solihull PHV test</a
        >
        and
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/solihull/how-to-apply/"
          >applying for a Solihull PHV licence</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>About the test</h2>

      <h3>How many questions are on the Solihull taxi badge test?</h3>

      <p>
        <strong>48 questions</strong> — 8 on each of the six subjects covered
        by the training course. You need <strong>36 correct (75%)</strong> to
        pass, and the test is allowed <strong>60 minutes</strong>.
      </p>

      <h3>Does the Solihull test have key questions like Wolverhampton?</h3>

      <p>
        No. Solihull marks the paper on your <strong>overall score
        alone</strong>. There is no set of key questions where a single wrong
        answer fails the whole paper — that rule belongs to
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/8-key-questions/"
          >Wolverhampton's test</a
        >, which is a different paper under different rules.
      </p>

      <h3>What format are the questions?</h3>

      <p>
        A <strong>combination of spoken, written and multiple-choice</strong>.
        Because part of it is spoken, being able to explain your reasoning
        matters — not just recognising the right option.
      </p>

      <h3>When do I get my result?</h3>

      <p>
        <strong>Within 5 working days.</strong> Your certificate needs to be
        less than 12 months old when you apply for your licence.
      </p>

      <h3>What happens if I fail?</h3>

      <p>
        Solihull states you may retake <strong>the whole course or just the
        test</strong>, and that a fee will be payable. The council doesn't
        publish that fee on its driver licence guide, so check the current
        amount with the licensing team.
      </p>

      <h2>About applying</h2>

      <h3>What DBS check do I need?</h3>

      <p>
        An <strong>enhanced</strong> disclosure — basic and standard are not
        accepted. It must be for the occupation of taxi/private hire driver
        under <strong>"other workforce"</strong> and include a check of both
        the adults' and children's barred lists. Solihull uses
        <strong>TaxiPlus</strong>, and you must subscribe to the DBS update
        service <strong>within 30 days</strong> of the certificate being
        issued.
      </p>

      <h3>What medical do I need?</h3>

      <p>
        You must meet <strong>DVLA Group 2 medical standards</strong>,
        assessed by a GMC registered medical practitioner on the council's own
        form. The certificate should be dated <strong>within 1 month</strong>
        of your application.
      </p>

      <h3>What is the Blue Lamp Trust assessment?</h3>

      <p>
        A <strong>practical driving assessment</strong> that Solihull requires
        before you apply, delivered by Blue Lamp Trust. The certificate needs
        to be <strong>less than 12 months old</strong> when you apply.
      </p>

      <h3>Do I need an HMRC tax check?</h3>

      <p>
        Only if you currently hold a private hire or hackney carriage licence,
        or held one within the last 12 months — those codes expire after
        <strong>120 days</strong>. If you've never held one, you sign a
        declaration confirming that instead.
      </p>

      <h3>How do I book my appointment?</h3>

      <p>
        Email
        <a href="mailto:licensing@solihull.gov.uk">licensing@solihull.gov.uk</a>
        with your full name, date of birth, mobile number and the reason for
        the appointment. <strong>Walk-ins are not accepted.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>About the app</h2>

      <h3>Are the practice questions specific to Solihull?</h3>

      <p>
        Yes. Every question in the app's Solihull mode is built from official
        Solihull Council source material — council policy documents, licensing
        handbooks and relevant UK legislation. This isn't generic PHV content.
      </p>

      <h3>Are the questions regularly updated?</h3>

      <p>
        Yes. Questions are updated as Solihull Council publishes new material,
        and Premium includes all future updates for life — no extra charge.
      </p>

      <h3>Will mock exams just repeat the same questions?</h3>

      <p>
        No. Each mock exam pulls 48 questions — 8 from each of the six
        categories — from the full 300+ question bank, so you get a different
        paper every time. All questions are distinct: no padding or rephrased
        duplicates.
      </p>

      <h3>Is this useful if I've already failed the test?</h3>

      <p>
        Especially then. The pass mark is 36 out of 48 (75%), and you need a
        solid spread across all six categories. The app tracks your score by
        category so you can see exactly where you're dropping marks and focus
        your revision there.
      </p>

      <h3>Do you have pass rate statistics?</h3>

      <p>
        No, and we won't invent one. We can't verify what happens after
        someone leaves the app and sits the real test. Anyone quoting you a
        percentage for something like this is guessing.
      </p>

      <p>
        PHV Prep UK is on
        <a
          href="https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/phv-prep-uk-taxi-badge-test/id6776364932"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">the App Store</a
        >
        and
        <a
          href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.phvprepuk.app&pcampaignid=web_share"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Google Play</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Official sources</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.solihull.gov.uk/business/licences/taxi-licensing"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">Solihull Council — Taxi licensing</a
